## Context

The analysis/writing workpackage split (`.claude/rules/coding-python.md`,
Build section) requires the writing build to compile from committed handoff
artifacts only — no `uv run`, no data access. This rule was violated in TWO
places, found one after the other:
- 0345: `make slides` triggered `uv run` (fixed)
- 0352: `make report` triggers `uv run` (to be fixed)

Two instances of the same shape means it is a class, not a one-off — it will
come back in an unrelated future PR. `/verify` is a per-PR gate; it will not
catch the class reappearing elsewhere. A standing adherence test will.

Blocked-by 0352: write this guard only after the report side is clean, so the
test passes on a green tree.

## Relevant files
- `Makefile` — root build; `make -n slides` / `make -n report` dry-run traces
- `tests/` — adherence tests live here (`@pytest.mark.adherence`)
- `.claude/rules/coding-python.md` — the rule being enforced

## Actions
1. Write an adherence test that runs `make -n slides` and `make -n report`
   (dry-run, no execution) and asserts no recipe line contains `uv run`.
2. Guard against the recursive-trigger variant too: ensure no
   `$(MAKE) -C ..` in `slides/Makefile` / `report/Makefile` re-enters root
   analysis rules. (Static grep of the sub-Makefiles is sufficient.)
3. Mark `@pytest.mark.adherence`. Keep it fast — dry-run + string match, no
   real build, no subprocess sleep. If it must spawn make, mark
   `@pytest.mark.integration` per the testing rules.

## Test
This ticket IS the test. Red step: before 0352 lands, the test fails on
`make -n report` (finds `uv run`). After 0352, it passes. Confirm it would
have failed pre-0345 too (catches the original slides leak).

## Verification
- [ ] Test fails when a `uv run` rule is introduced into a writing-build path
- [ ] Test passes on current main (after 0352)
- [ ] `pytest -m adherence` runs it in < 30s

## Invariants
- Test must catch the class, not just the two known instances — phrase the
  assertion over the dry-run recipe trace, not a hardcoded rule list

## Exit criteria
- An adherence test asserts `make slides` and `make report` invoke no
  `uv run` / data-access commands
- `make check` passes
